# Under testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime the yes of `$findsNoMember` as the library writes it is asked of the object. Under testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime the compiler tests what it remembers of the cell, in front of the question, by a record of the same kind: its yes says
# "no field outside its slot, the layout's prototype", not "a lookup finds nothing". Here the prototype holds the name: the written question says no, rightly, and the compiler's own record says yes, rightly. A net that takes every record of the kind stops both runs.
# RUN(BEFORE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,CheckWalkAtRunTime give = () => "missing"; keep = x => x; later = function () { };
